      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The swelling and potential instability are due to the violent chemical reaction between lithium ions and the electrolyte in the battery during charging cycles. This reaction causes the battery to swell due to the release of gases, primarily oxygen and hydrogen, which can build up pressure. When these gases are released too quickly or under too much pressure, they can lead to a thermal runaway, causing the battery to overheat, short circuit, or even catch fire.",
